  },
  {
    "id": 10,
    "text": "To make a wooden copy, lay the chosen drawing face up over a separate transfer sheet and a blank block, with the top edges aligned. Trace the outlines and carve away the background. The raised wooden design matches the drawing as you viewed it. The original paper is not cut.\n\nTo make a reversed guide, hold the master against the lit window with its printed face toward the glass. Trace the design seen through its back onto a fresh sheet.\n\nPrinting reverses a block's raised face onto paper. Ink either block and take a proof to check it. The workbench has enough paper, transfer sheets and blank blocks to try both versions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4286,
        "world": "copy-workroom-locations-v2",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "stock",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
